('key', [
    "**Stress** = the non-specific response of the body to any demand (**Selye, 1936**); psychologically, demand exceeding perceived coping ability. **Perception is central.**",
    "**Eustress** (positive, motivating) vs **distress** (negative, harmful); also hyperstress, hypostress, acute, episodic acute, chronic and traumatic stress.",
    "**Yerkes\u2013Dodson law** \u2014 inverted-U: performance is best at an **optimum** level of arousal. The goal is optimisation, not elimination.",
    "**GAS = Alarm \u2192 Resistance \u2192 Exhaustion** (Selye). Adrenaline/noradrenaline acutely; **cortisol** via the **HPA axis**; 'diseases of adaptation' in exhaustion.",
    "**Fight-or-flight** and **homeostasis** \u2014 Walter Cannon. **Allostatic load** = cumulative wear of chronic stress.",
    "Effects are **physical, emotional, cognitive, behavioural and interpersonal**; chronic stress causes hypertension, CAD, diabetes, peptic ulcer, immunosuppression, insomnia, anxiety and depression.",
    "**Burnout (Maslach) = Emotional exhaustion + Depersonalisation/cynicism + Reduced personal accomplishment**; classified by WHO ICD-11 as an **occupational phenomenon**.",
    "**Burnout is work-specific; depression is pervasive.** Compassion fatigue arises from empathic exposure to suffering.",
    "Coping: **problem-focused** (when the stressor is controllable \u2014 most effective), **emotion-focused** (when it is not), meaning-focused, social support; and **maladaptive/avoidant** (alcohol, denial, withdrawal), which must be replaced.",
    "Relaxation techniques: deep/diaphragmatic breathing, **Jacobson's PMR**, meditation, **MBSR mindfulness**, yoga and *pranayama*, guided imagery, autogenic training, biofeedback, music, laughter therapy, 5-4-3-2-1 grounding.",
    "**Organisational measures matter more than individual ones** \u2014 staffing, rosters, autonomy, just culture, recognition, safety, POSH committee, occupational health and counselling.",
    "**Stress management is a patient-safety measure**, because stress and burnout increase error."
]),

